[119.1509, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[3;4Hjpterm execute hunt.ipynb --cell enrich                                                         \r\n \u001b[33m$\u001b[m \u001b[1mShell \u001b[mRun detection cell 20 lines…\r\n   jpterm execute hunt.ipynb --cell detection                   \r\n\r\n \u001b[34m●\u001b[m \u001b[1mFinding:\u001b[m \u001b[37m 198.51.100.22 \u001b[m is a confirmed low-and-slow password spray.\r\n\r\n   • \u001b[1mScale:\u001b[m it ran from Sep 07 to Nov 24 against 335 accounts, over 13 days that each crossed the rule.\r\n   • \u001b[1mIntel:\u001b[m the community feed lists it as \"password spraying\", first reported Sep 04.\r\n   • \u001b[1mCompromise:\u001b[m it signed in successfully as \u001b[37m svc_backup \u001b[m (backup operator) on Nov 22 at 03:12. I'd treat\r\n\u001b[5Cthat account as compromised.\r\n   • \u001b[1mFalse positive:\u001b[m \u001b[37m 203.0.113.7 \u001b[m is not a spray, because at most 10% of its sign-ins fail.      \u001b[5C     \r\n   • \u001b[1mCaveat:\u001b[m setup said \u001b[37m lake: fixture (not the lake) \u001b[m, so these cell results may come from fixture data.\r\n\u001b[5CConfirm they match the real lake before acting.\r\n\u001b[108C\u001b[1"]
[119.150913, "o", "K\r\n   \u001b[1mNext steps (your call):\u001b[m                        \r\n\r\n   1. Reset \u001b[37m svc_backup \u001b[m credentials, kill its sessions, and review what it did after Nov 22 03:12.  \r\n   2. Block \u001b[37m 198.51.100.22 \u001b[m and check the other accounts it signed in to, if any.                          \r\n   3. Create the daily saved search from the \u001b[37m detection \u001b[m SQL. The notebook's SQL is a one-off over a fixed\r\n\u001b[6Cwindow, so scheduling it over a rolling 24h or 7d range is a design choice for you. Per the project\r\n\u001b[5C\u001b[1K rules it would be named \u001b[37m demo_… \u001b[m in the \u001b[37m search \u001b[m app via \u001b[37m splunkctl \u001b[m, and I'd show you the command\r\n      before any write.                   \r\n\u001b[108C\u001b[1K\r\n   Want me to draft the \u001b[37m splunkctl \u001b[m command for step 3?\r\u001b[6B \u001b[1m←\u001b[m open sidebar · Interactive · Manual Approval · \u001b[1m/\u001b[m commands · \u001b[1m?\u001b[m help · \u001b[1mtab\u001b[m next tab\u001b[30;3H\u001b[?25h"]
